# Cross-Origin Resource Sharing

[Cross-Origin Resource Sharing (CORS)](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Guides/CORS) lets a server tell browsers which other origins may read its responses. It's a browser security mechanism, not authentication, and it doesn't stop requests from `curl`, server-side programs, or other non-browser clients.

![CORS Explainer](/media/storage.googleapis.com/qvault-webapp-dynamic-assets/lesson_videos/CORS-1920x1080.mp4){captions="captions.vtt"}

## Preflight

For some cross-origin requests, the browser sends a [preflight](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Glossary/Preflight_request) `OPTIONS` request before the real request. The response needs to approve the requesting origin, method, and any non-safelisted headers. Otherwise, the browser refuses to send the actual request.

Requests that don't require preflight may still be sent, but JavaScript can't read their responses unless the server grants access.

## Bearly Secure's CORS Bug

Bearly Secure reflects every requesting `Origin` into `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` and sends `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true`. Instead of limiting access, that policy tells the browser that any website asking for authenticated data may read it.

An attacker's page can make a credentialed request:

```js
const response = await fetch("http://localhost:3030/api/account", {
  credentials: "include",
});
const account = await response.json();
```

The same-origin policy would normally block the attacker from reading the response. Bearly Secure's CORS headers explicitly grant that origin access, so the browser exposes the authenticated data to the attacker's JavaScript.

# Global Error Handling

A safe error response is useless if one forgotten handler lets a panic escape. In Go, recovery middleware gives you one final boundary between unexpected failures and public responses.

Install a deferred function before calling the next handler. If downstream code panics, [`recover`](https://go.dev/ref/spec#Handling_panics) can capture the value so the middleware can log it and return a generic response:

```go
func recoverPanics(next http.Handler) http.Handler {
    return http.HandlerFunc(func(responseWriter http.ResponseWriter, request *http.Request) {
        defer func() {
            if recovered := recover(); recovered != nil {
                slog.Error("unhandled panic", "value", recovered)
                http.Error(responseWriter, "Something went wrong", http.StatusInternalServerError)
            }
        }()

        next.ServeHTTP(responseWriter, request)
    })
}
```

Some failures are expected or handler-specific and _should be handled_ where they occur. A missing concert ticket should get a deliberate `404`, and invalid checkout input should get a client-safe `400`. Recovery middleware is a last resort for unexpected panics, not a replacement for ordinary error handling.

> [!tip]
>
> Handle expected failures locally. Use recovery middleware to log unexpected panics and return a safe `500`.

steps.command:
awk '
  /^[[:space:]]*#/ { next }
  toupper($1) == "FROM" {
    stages++
    if (golang) earlierGo = 1
    golang = ($0 ~ /(^|[[:space:]\/])golang:/)
    alpine = ($0 ~ /(^|[[:space:]\/])alpine:/)
  }
  END {
    print "Multiple stages: " (stages >= 2 ? "yes" : "no")
    print "Earlier Go build stage: " (earlierGo ? "yes" : "no")
    print "Final Alpine runtime stage: " (alpine ? "yes" : "no")
  }
' Dockerfile

awk '
  /^[[:space:]]*#/ { next }
  /\\[[:space:]]*$/ { sub(/\\[[:space:]]*$/, ""); pending = pending $0 " "; next }
  {
    $0 = pending $0
    pending = ""
    if (toupper($1) == "FROM") {
      golang = ($0 ~ /(^|[[:space:]\/])golang:/)
      staticEnv = 0
      copiedInputs = 0
    }
    if (!golang) next
    if (toupper($1) == "COPY" || toupper($1) == "ADD") copiedInputs = 1
    if (toupper($1) == "ENV" && /CGO_ENABLED/) {
      staticEnv = ($0 ~ /CGO_ENABLED[[:space:]=]+["\047]?0(["\047[:space:]]|$)/)
    }
    if (toupper($1) != "RUN" || $0 !~ /go[[:space:]]+build/) next
    staticBuild = copiedInputs && (staticEnv || ($0 ~ /CGO_ENABLED[[:space:]=]+["\047]?0(["\047[:space:]]|$)/))
    if (staticBuild && /cmd\/server([\/"\047[:space:];&]|$)/) server = 1
    if (staticBuild && /cmd\/attackerlab([\/"\047[:space:];&]|$)/) attacker = 1
  }
  END {
    print "Static server build requested: " (server ? "yes" : "no")
    print "Static attacker-lab build requested: " (attacker ? "yes" : "no")
  }
' Dockerfile

awk '
  /^[[:space:]]*#/ { next }
  /\\[[:space:]]*$/ { sub(/\\[[:space:]]*$/, ""); pending = pending $0 " "; next }
  {
    $0 = pending $0
    pending = ""
    if (toupper($1) == "FROM") {
      fromBuild = assetsWeb = assetsLab = pdf = broadCopy = certificates = 0
    }
    if (toupper($1) == "RUN" && /apk/ && /add/ && /ca-certificates/) certificates = 1
    if (toupper($1) != "COPY" && toupper($1) != "ADD") next
    if (/--from[=[:space:]]/) fromBuild = 1
    if (/(^|[\/[:space:]"\047])web([\/[:space:]"\047]|$)/) assetsWeb = 1
    if (/(^|[\/[:space:]"\047])attacker-lab([\/[:space:]"\047]|$)/) assetsLab = 1
    if (/mystery-shack-tax-exemption\.pdf/) pdf = 1
    gsub(/[\[\]",]/, " ")
    for (i = 2; i < NF; i++) {
      source = $i
      if (source ~ /^--/) continue
      gsub(/\047/, "", source)
      sub(/\/+$/, "", source)
      while (source ~ /^\.\//) sub(/^\.\//, "", source)
      if (source == "." || source == "" || source == "*") broadCopy = 1
    }
  }
  END {
    print "Copy from another stage: " (fromBuild ? "yes" : "no")
    print "Web assets copied: " (assetsWeb ? "yes" : "no")
    print "Attacker-lab assets copied: " (assetsLab ? "yes" : "no")
    print "Required PDF copied: " (pdf ? "yes" : "no")
    print "No whole-project runtime copy: " (!broadCopy ? "yes" : "no")
    print "CA certificates installation requested: " (certificates ? "yes" : "no")
  }
' Dockerfile

awk '
  /^[[:space:]]*#/ { next }
  /\\[[:space:]]*$/ { sub(/\\[[:space:]]*$/, ""); pending = pending $0 " "; next }
  {
    $0 = pending $0
    pending = ""
    instruction = toupper($1)
    if (instruction == "FROM") user = ownership = startup = ""
    if (instruction == "USER") {
      user = $2
      gsub(/["\047]/, "", user)
      sub(/:.*/, "", user)
    }
    if ((instruction == "RUN" && /chown/) || ((instruction == "COPY" || instruction == "ADD") && /--chown=/)) {
      if (/(^|[\/[:space:]"\047])data([\/[:space:]"\047]|$)/) ownership = 1
    }
    if (instruction == "CMD" || instruction == "ENTRYPOINT") startup = 1
  }
  END {
    print "Final non-root USER selected: " (user != "" && tolower(user) != "root" && user !~ /^0+$/ ? "yes" : "no")
    print "Data ownership configured: " (ownership ? "yes" : "no")
    print "Runtime startup configured: " (startup ? "yes" : "no")
  }
' Dockerfile

